   {:id "L2" :owner :host :statement "A finite field has at least one coordinate; an empty finite field is refused before a generator is built." :evidence "TypeLattice.create/applyGuard; generator refusals"}
   {:id "L3" :owner :host :statement "A numeric coordinate or threshold is representable on its sort; integer and natural values are integral and Int32-bounded." :evidence "DomainExpression.integerValue/naturalValue; TypeLattice.validateThreshold"}
   {:id "L4" :owner :host :statement "Narrowing is monotone and idempotent." :evidence "TypeLattice.applyGuard; withGuards; tests"}
   {:id "L5" :owner :host :statement "Product composition concatenates fields and validates; duplicate field names are refused." :evidence "TypeLattice.product; property lattice-product-composes"}
   {:id "L6" :owner :host :statement "Constraints are the distinct narrowing guards in field order; the document guard is not conjoined twice." :evidence "TypeLattice.constraints; Smt.precondition; emitter tests"}
   {:id "L7" :owner :host :statement "The emitter refuses a lattice narrowing that the document does not carry." :evidence "Emitter.emitFSharp/emitSmt divergence checks"}
   {:id "L8" :owner :host :statement "A symbolic field can feed Z3 but not a finite generator or exhaustive refiner; the refusal is named." :evidence "coordinatesAfterNarrowing; candidateGuards; refiner tests"}
   {:id "L9" :owner :host :statement "A named guard without a resolver is undecided or refused, never silently false." :evidence "GuardResolver; D41 tests"}
   {:id "L10" :owner :host :statement "The lattice is a pure value; direct construction must call validate before a reader." :evidence "public Field/Lattice; validate; pure-lattice tests"}
   {:id "L11" :owner :host :statement "Sum composition is data-shaped only; execution is refused until a tagged-union reader semantics exists." :evidence "TypeLattice.composition; refusal list; no sum execution"}]
  :row-types
  [{:id "R1" :owner :both :statement "Closed rows with the same labels unify; different closed labels are refused." :evidence "RowTypes tests"}
   {:id "R2" :owner :both :statement "An open row absorbs the other side's labels." :evidence "RowTypes tests"}
   {:id "R3" :owner :both :statement "Two open rows meet at a fresh common tail." :evidence "RowTypes tests"}
   {:id "R4" :owner :both :statement "A row variable cannot occur in itself; duplicate labels are refused." :evidence "RowTypes tests"}]
